{
  "about": "Reference leads for mapping call types to the taxonomy in taxonomy.json. People, numbers and answers are invented (555-01xx numbers, example.com). Call types are real contact-type names used by many firms, or invented ones where a case needs a person's name. Intake labels are the real question wording firms use for that practice area. 'expect' is what the rules must return; tools/call_categories.py fails if any lead maps differently. 'crm' is the category's default: send (deliver to the firm's CRM), skip (a message, not a lead), review (the firm decides), never (not a kind of call).",
